+### Subscription State Query and Change Notification
+
+**Key Points**:
+- `get_subscription_state()` returns the current `SubscriptionState` synchronously and may be called at any time.
+- `set_subscription_state_change_handler()` registers a callback invoked whenever the state changes; an existing handler is replaced silently.
+- Returning `false` from the handler unregisters it (same effect as `unset_subscription_state_change_handler()`).
+- The handler may run on a middleware thread while an internal lock is held: keep it short and do not call back into the same subscription (this may deadlock).
+
+<details>
+<summary>Examples:</summary>
+
+```rust
+use score_com::{Result, Runtime, Subscription, SubscriptionState};
+use com_api_gen::Tire;
+
+// Query the current subscription state (can be called at any time)
+fn report_state<R: Runtime>(subscription: &impl Subscription<Tire, R>) -> SubscriptionState {
+    subscription.get_subscription_state()
+}
+
+// Register a state-change notification and unregister it later
+fn watch_state<R: Runtime>(subscription: &impl Subscription<Tire, R>) -> Result<()> {
+    subscription.set_subscription_state_change_handler(|new_state| {
+        println!("subscription state changed to {new_state:?}");
+        true // keep the handler registered; return false to unregister it
+    })?;
+
+    // ... later, if needed:
+    subscription.unset_subscription_state_change_handler()?;
+    Ok(())
+}
+```
+</details>
+
